cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Deterministic guardrails for LLM narratives in a FHIR-based Alzheimer's neuroimaging CDSS (code)"
abstract: >-
  Code for a deterministic closed-loop guardrail that keeps LLM-written narratives and question answering
  factual over the frozen explainable-AI output of a 2.5D MobileViT Alzheimer's classifier, a translator of the
  audited narrative into HL7 FHIR R4, and a clinical decision support system (CDSS) interface. Research
  prototype, not a medical device. Synthetic demonstration data only.
authors:
  - family-names: Widjaja
    given-names: Jonathan Albertus
  - family-names: Hareva
    given-names: David Habsara
repository-code: "https://github.com/nathanwidjaja10/alzheimer-cdss-guardrails"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
keywords:
  - deterministic guardrails
  - large language models
  - HL7 FHIR
  - neuroimaging
  - clinical decision support
  - Alzheimer's disease
